---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[narrow_pointers]: this changes the high half of a 64-bit pointer: the bits do not exist on 32-bit targets
  --> tests/lint/narrow_pointers/bad.jai:10:13
   |
10 |     return (cast(u64) node) >> 48;
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a pointer is 4 bytes on 32-bit targets: keep tags in the low bits, or store them next to the pointer
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/narrow_pointers

warning[narrow_pointers]: this changes the high half of a 64-bit pointer: the bits do not exist on 32-bit targets
  --> tests/lint/narrow_pointers/bad.jai:14:13
   |
14 |     return (cast(u64) node) & 0x0000_ffff_ffff_ffff;
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a pointer is 4 bytes on 32-bit targets: keep tags in the low bits, or store them next to the pointer
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/narrow_pointers

warning[narrow_pointers]: this changes the high half of a 64-bit pointer: the bits do not exist on 32-bit targets
  --> tests/lint/narrow_pointers/bad.jai:18:13
   |
18 |     return (cast(u64) node) | 0x8000_0000_0000_0000;
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: a pointer is 4 bytes on 32-bit targets: keep tags in the low bits, or store them next to the pointer
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/narrow_pointers

warning[narrow_pointers]: this reads a pointer as a 64-bit integer: it is 4 bytes on 32-bit targets
  --> tests/lint/narrow_pointers/bad.jai:23:12
   |
23 |     return cast(*u64) slot;
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: read the pointer through its own type
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/narrow_pointers

warning[narrow_pointers]: the address 0x100000000 does not fit in a 32-bit pointer
  --> tests/lint/narrow_pointers/bad.jai:27:12
   |
27 |     return cast(*Node) cast(u64) 0x1_0000_0000;
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: use a value below 2^32, or build the pointer from a variable
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/narrow_pointers
